            return -1;
        }
    }

    free(buffer);
    return 0;
}
```
This code uses a `try-catch` block to handle any exceptions that may occur during the allocation and deallocation of memory. If an exception occurs, the program will catch it and release any allocated memory before exiting with an error message. This ensures that the program does not leak memory in the event of an error.']

